{{- /*
page.gohtml is the shop's one shell.

Three pages render it and differ only in the mount's id, which is what the script
branches on. The values the script needs — the publishable key, the sales channel
and the product handle — travel as DATA ATTRIBUTES rather than inside the script,
so the script stays one file with one stamp for every installation.

The noscript block is not a courtesy. Every figure on this page arrives by fetch,
so a shopper whose script did not run sees an empty box, and an empty shop is
indistinguishable from a broken one.
*/ -}}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>{{ .Title }}</title>
<style>
  body { font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif; margin: 0 auto; max-width: 46rem; padding: 1.5rem; }
  header { display: flex; gap: 1rem; align-items: baseline; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 0; }
  a { color: inherit; }
  ul { list-style: none; padding: 0; }
  li { border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.75rem 0; }
  .muted { color: #666; }
  .notice { background: #fffbe6; border: 1px solid #e8d98a; padding: 0.75rem; }
  button { font: inherit; padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<header>
  <h1><a href="{{ .Paths.List }}">Shop</a></h1>
  <span class="muted"><a href="{{ .Paths.Cart }}">Cart</a></span>
</header>

<noscript>
  <p class="notice">This shop reads the catalog from /store/v1 in the browser and needs JavaScript.</p>
</noscript>

<main id="shop"
      data-mount="{{ .Mount }}"
      data-handle="{{ .Handle }}"
      data-key="{{ .Key }}"
      data-channel="{{ .Channel }}"
      data-cart-path="{{ .Paths.Cart }}"
      data-list-path="{{ .Paths.List }}">
  <p class="muted">Loading…</p>
</main>

<script src="{{ .Script }}" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
